# Team Work & Sprint Management System
## Complete Functional Workflow & Product Specification

**Version:** 1.0  
**Application:** Web-based Team Work & Sprint Management System  
**Frontend:** React + TypeScript  
**Backend:** Node.js + Express  
**Initial Data Store:** Google Sheets  
**Authentication:** Google Workspace Sign-In  
**User Roles:** Admin and Member

---

# 1. Product Overview

The Team Work & Sprint Management System is a centralized platform for managing daily employee activities, working hours, individual assignments, sprint progress and team productivity.

The application should provide a simple, transparent and reliable workflow where every team member can record their daily work, track time spent, update progress and submit their daily report.

Administrators should have complete visibility into team activities, working hours, sprint execution, pending submissions and productivity insights.

The system should minimize manual follow-ups through automated validations, reminders and carry-forward workflows.

## 1.1 Primary Objectives

- Track daily work activities for every team member.
- Allow multiple work entries per person per day.
- Track actual working hours against configurable expected hours.
- Maintain daily work progress and completion status.
- Manage weekly sprints, tickets and assignments.
- Automatically carry forward incomplete work.
- Enforce mandatory daily submissions.
- Send automated EOD reminders.
- Provide team-wide working-hour visibility.
- Maintain a complete audit history.
- Provide meaningful team and sprint performance insights.

## 1.2 Core Decisions

| Configuration | Decision |
|---|---|
| Expected daily working hours | Customizable |
| EOD reminder | 20:00 |
| Daily submission | Strict / Mandatory |
| Admin approval | Not required |
| Incomplete work | Automatic carry-forward |
| Working hours visibility | Entire team |
| Authentication | Google Workspace |
| User roles | Admin and Member |
| Initial database | Google Sheets |
| Application architecture | React + API backend |

All time-based operations must use a configurable company timezone.

