# 2. User Roles & Access Management

The system supports two roles.

## 2.1 Admin

Administrators have complete access to the system.

**Responsibilities:**

- Manage team members.
- Assign and modify user roles.
- Configure working hours and working days.
- Create and manage sprints.
- Create, assign and manage tickets.
- View all team members' daily activities.
- Monitor working hours and productivity.
- View daily submission statuses.
- Monitor blockers and delayed work.
- Configure holidays and leave.
- View reminder delivery statuses.
- Access audit logs.
- Generate team and sprint reports.
- Correct or reopen submitted daily reports through an audited process.

## 2.2 Member

Members can manage their own daily work and view team-level information.

**Responsibilities:**

- Sign in using their office Google account.
- View their daily dashboard.
- Add multiple work entries per day.
- Update their work progress.
- Record start and end times.
- Add comments and blockers.
- View their work history.
- View their assigned tickets and sprint.
- Submit their daily report.
- View team working-hour summaries.
- View team sprint progress.

Members cannot:

- Modify another member's work.
- Change their own role.
- Modify system settings.
- Change expected working hours.
- Modify sprint configurations.
- Edit audit logs.
- Reopen a submitted day without an authorized correction process.

