# 6. My Work – Daily Work Management

This is the primary feature of the application.

A member can add multiple work entries for the same day.

Each entry represents a separate activity or task.

## 6.1 Add Work Workflow

1. Member opens the My Work section.
2. Selects "Add Work".
3. Enters work details.
4. Selects the category.
5. Records start and end times.
6. Updates the progress percentage.
7. Selects the work status.
8. Adds comments or additional notes.
9. Saves the entry.

## 6.2 Work Entry Fields

| Field | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Work ID | Automatically generated |
| Work Date | Required |
| Work Title | Required |
| Description | Recommended |
| Category | Required |
| Ticket ID | Optional |
| Sprint ID | Optional |
| Start Time | Required |
| End Time | Required |
| Duration | Automatically calculated |
| Progress | 0–100% |
| Status | Required |
| Comments | Optional |
| Blocker Details | Required when blocked |
| Next Action | Required when blocked |
| Created By | Automatically populated |
| Created At | Automatically populated |
| Updated At | Automatically populated |

## 6.3 Work Categories

- Development
- Bug Fix
- Code Review
- Testing / QA
- Meeting
- Technical Discussion
- Support
- Research
- Documentation
- Deployment
- Other

Administrators should be able to manage the category list.

## 6.4 Work Statuses

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Not Started | Work has not started |
| In Progress | Work is ongoing |
| Blocked | Work cannot proceed |
| Completed | Work is finished |
| Carried Forward | Incomplete work moved to another working day |
| Deferred | Work intentionally postponed |

## 6.5 Progress Tracking

Every work entry must have a progress value between 0% and 100%.

Rules:

- New work defaults to 0%.
- Progress must be updated by the member.
- Completed status requires 100%.
- 100% progress automatically changes the status to Completed.
- A Completed task cannot be marked as In Progress without an explicit audited reopening.
- Blocked work must contain blocker details and a next action.

**Completion principle:** The system must encourage members to complete their assigned work to 100%. However, it must never artificially mark unfinished work as completed just to satisfy daily submission. Incomplete work remains visible and is automatically carried forward.

