# 7. Working Hours & Time Tracking

Working hours must be calculated from individual work entries.

## 7.1 Time Calculation

Duration = End Time − Start Time.

Example:

| Work | Start | End | Duration |
|---|---|---|---:|
| Development | 09:00 | 11:00 | 2 hours |
| Bug Fix | 11:15 | 12:45 | 1.5 hours |
| Meeting | 13:30 | 14:30 | 1 hour |
| Code Review | 14:45 | 17:15 | 2.5 hours |
| **Total** | | | **7 hours** |

The system should automatically calculate:

- Daily logged hours.
- Expected hours.
- Remaining hours.
- Excess hours.
- Weekly logged hours.
- Sprint-period logged hours.

## 7.2 Expected Working Hours

Expected hours must be configurable.

Administrators can configure:

- Default daily working hours.
- Individual member working hours.
- Working days.
- Effective dates for schedule changes.
- Date-specific expected-hour overrides.

For example:

| Member | Expected Hours |
|---|---:|
| Member A | 8 hours |
| Member B | 7.5 hours |
| Member C | 6 hours |

## 7.3 Working Hour Visibility

All team members can view the team's logged working hours.

Members can see:

- Their own detailed work entries.
- Their own total hours.
- Team member names and daily hour totals.
- Team-level weekly hour summaries.

Detailed personal descriptions and private notes should not automatically become visible to the entire team. Admins have full authorized access.

