# 8. Daily Submission – Strict Workflow

Daily submission is mandatory on every scheduled working day.

There is no Admin approval workflow.

## 8.1 Submission Process

1. Member records their daily activities.
2. System calculates total working hours.
3. System checks all work entries.
4. System validates required information.
5. Member reviews the daily summary.
6. Member selects "Submit Daily Report".
7. Backend validates the report again.
8. Submission is saved with a timestamp.
9. The day is marked as Submitted.
10. Member receives a confirmation message.

## 8.2 Submission Validation

Before allowing submission, validate:

- At least one work entry exists, or a valid no-work reason is provided.
- Every entry has a valid title and category.
- All time ranges are valid.
- No time entries overlap.
- Every entry has a valid progress value.
- Completed entries have 100% progress.
- Blocked entries include blocker details and next action.
- Required comments and descriptions are present according to configured rules.
- The daily total is calculated correctly.
- Any working-hour shortfall or excess has an explanation where required.

If no work was performed, the member must provide a meaningful reason.

## 8.3 Submission Lock

After successful submission:

- Normal editing is disabled.
- The submitted report becomes read-only.
- The member can view the submitted report.
- Any correction requires an Admin-authorized reopen or correction action.
- The system records the original values, modified values, actor and timestamp.

Submission status and task completion status must remain separate.

