# 9. Automatic Carry-Forward

Incomplete work must automatically move to the next applicable working day.

## 9.1 Carry-Forward Conditions

A work entry is eligible when:

- Its progress is below 100%.
- Its status is not Completed.
- It is not intentionally Deferred or Cancelled.
- It has not already been carried forward to the target day.

## 9.2 Carry-Forward Workflow

1. Scheduled backend job checks incomplete work.
2. System identifies the next working day.
3. Weekends and configured holidays are skipped.
4. A new daily work entry is created.
5. Original work ID is retained as the source reference.
6. Existing progress is preserved.
7. Previous comments and history remain accessible.
8. New-day time tracking starts empty.
9. The member sees the carried-forward item on their dashboard.

## 9.3 Example

| Day | Work | Progress |
|---|---|---:|
| Monday | API Integration | 40% |
| Tuesday | API Integration | 65% |
| Wednesday | API Integration | 100% |

The same logical work continues across days without losing its history.

The system must not add the previous day's hours to the new day's hours.

## 9.4 Carry-Forward Controls

- Carry-forward must be idempotent.
- Duplicate carry-forward records must be prevented.
- Completed work must never be carried forward.
- Deferred work must follow its explicit rescheduling date.
- Repeated carry-forward should be highlighted in reports.
- Admins must be able to inspect the carry-forward history.

