# 10. Sprint Management

Administrators manage sprint planning and execution.

The system should support weekly or configurable sprint durations.

## 10.1 Create Sprint

Required fields:

- Sprint ID.
- Sprint Name.
- Start Date.
- End Date.
- Sprint Goal.
- Sprint Status.

Sprint statuses:

- Planned
- Active
- Completed
- Cancelled

## 10.2 Sprint Workflow

1. Admin creates a sprint.
2. Admin defines the sprint goal.
3. Admin creates tickets.
4. Admin assigns tickets to members.
5. Members view their assigned tickets.
6. Members record daily work against tickets.
7. Ticket progress is updated.
8. System calculates sprint progress.
9. Admin reviews blockers and unfinished work.
10. Sprint is closed after completion.

## 10.3 Sprint Metrics

- Total tickets.
- Completed tickets.
- In-progress tickets.
- Blocked tickets.
- Deferred tickets.
- Sprint completion percentage.
- Work carried forward.
- Member-wise workload.
- Estimated versus actual effort.
- Tickets completed within the sprint.

Sprint progress should be calculated using ticket estimates when estimates are available and consistently populated. Otherwise, use an equal-ticket weighting method.

