# 13. Automated Email Workflows

Email notifications should reduce manual follow-ups.

## 13.1 EOD Reminder

**Scheduled time:** 20:00 company timezone.

Every scheduled working day, the system checks daily submissions.

If a member has not submitted their report, the system sends a reminder.

**Email subject:** Reminder: Please submit your daily work report

**Email content:**

Hi [Member Name],

This is a friendly reminder to submit your daily work report for [Date].

Please make sure all your work activities, progress updates and working hours are recorded before submitting your daily report.

If you did not perform any work today, please submit the report with an appropriate reason.

Thank you.

Team Work Tracker

## 13.2 Reminder Rules

- Only active members are eligible.
- Only scheduled working days are considered.
- Holidays and approved leave are excluded.
- Already-submitted reports are excluded.
- Each member receives at most one successful EOD reminder per date.
- Failed deliveries are logged and retried according to the configured retry policy.
- Submission after the reminder suppresses further reminders.
- Admins can view reminder delivery status.

## 13.3 Other Notification Events

| Event | Recipient |
|---|---|
| Daily reminder | Member |
| Daily submission confirmation | Member |
| Work assigned | Assigned member |
| Ticket due date approaching | Assigned member |
| Ticket overdue | Member and Admin |
| Work marked Blocked | Admin and relevant stakeholders |
| Sprint started | Sprint members |
| Sprint nearing completion | Admin and sprint members |
| Member account activated | Member |
| Member account deactivated | Admin |

Notifications should be configurable so that unnecessary email volume can be avoided.

