# 14. Additional Validation & Business Rules

The system should enforce the following checks consistently at the API level.

## 14.1 Work Entry Validation

- Work title cannot be empty.
- Work title must meet a minimum length.
- Work date must be valid.
- Start time must be earlier than end time.
- Duration must be positive.
- Overlapping work entries are not allowed.
- Progress must remain between 0 and 100.
- Completed work requires 100%.
- Blocked work requires a blocker description and next action.
- Duplicate entries should be flagged where appropriate.
- Members cannot create work on behalf of another member.

## 14.2 Daily Submission Validation

- Only one active submission per member per date.
- Daily submission is mandatory on working days.
- No-work submissions require a meaningful reason.
- Submitted reports are locked.
- Corrections require an Admin action and audit event.
- Late submissions must be identified separately.
- Working-hour deviations must be highlighted.

## 14.3 Working Hour Validation

- No overlapping time entries.
- Missing start or end times are rejected.
- Unusually long workdays are flagged.
- Very short workdays are flagged.
- Working-hour shortfalls require an explanation.
- Excess hours are highlighted without automatically treating them as overtime.
- Expected hours must respect individual schedules and date overrides.

## 14.4 Sprint Validation

- Sprint dates must be valid.
- Sprint end date cannot precede the start date.
- Tickets must reference valid sprints.
- Inactive members cannot receive new assignments.
- Completed tickets must have 100% progress.
- Overdue and stale tickets must be highlighted.

## 14.5 Account Validation

- Only verified company Google accounts are accepted.
- Inactive accounts cannot sign in.
- Roles are assigned by the backend.
- Role changes must be audited.
- Deactivated users' historical records must be retained according to the retention policy.

