# 15. Audit Logging

All important system operations must be recorded in an append-only audit log.

## 15.1 Events to Audit

- User sign-in.
- User activation and deactivation.
- Role changes.
- Working-hour configuration changes.
- Sprint creation and modification.
- Ticket creation and assignment.
- Work entry creation.
- Work entry modification.
- Work status changes.
- Progress changes.
- Daily submission.
- Daily report reopening.
- Daily report correction.
- Carry-forward operations.
- Reminder email attempts.
- System configuration changes.

## 15.2 Audit Record Structure

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| Audit ID | Unique event ID |
| Actor | User or system |
| Action | Operation performed |
| Entity Type | Work, Ticket, Sprint, Member, etc. |
| Entity ID | Affected record |
| Before Values | Previous state |
| After Values | Updated state |
| Timestamp | Event time |
| Source | User action or automated process |

Audit history must not be editable by normal Admin or Member interfaces.

Direct spreadsheet access must be restricted to authorized administrators and the backend service account.

