# 20. Security, Reliability & Operational Requirements

- HTTPS must be enforced in production.
- Google identity tokens must be verified server-side.
- Backend sessions must be securely managed.
- Secrets must be stored in environment variables or a secret manager.
- Service account credentials must never be exposed to the browser.
- API endpoints must enforce role-based access control.
- Inputs must be validated on the server.
- Rate limiting must protect authentication and write endpoints.
- CORS must allow only approved frontend origins.
- Spreadsheet access must be restricted.
- Backups and recovery procedures must be established.
- Application logs must avoid exposing credentials or unnecessary personal data.
- Employee work-hour visibility and retention must comply with company policies.

For the initial Google Sheets deployment, use a single controlled backend writer or implement a reliable write queue and locking mechanism. Avoid multiple independent application instances writing concurrently without coordination.

